. predict mgale, mgale
{txt}
{com}. 
. *Plots
. *energy
. twoway (scatter mgale energy) (lowess mgale energy )
{res}{txt}
{com}. 
. * energy: lowess of martingale residuals declines roughly linearly from 2 to 3.7 (1000 kcal/day), flattening above 3.7 where data are sparse; approximately linear, but to be later compared to other forms
. 
. 
. *height
. twoway (scatter mgale ht) (lowess mgale ht )
{res}{txt}
{com}. ** Height: the lowess line is not linear (nearly flat from about 163 to 176 cm, then falling steeply), so height will be categorized at 178 cm, where the fall begins
. 
. *weight
. twoway (scatter mgale wt) (lowess mgale wt )
{res}{txt}
{com}. ** Weight: the lowess line is not linear (flat at about 50-55 kg, falling from about 57 kg, then flat again above about 73 kg), so weight will be categorized at 60 kg, where the fall starts
. 
. *bmi
. twoway (scatter mgale bmi) (lowess mgale bmi)
{res}{txt}
{com}. *non linear 
. 
. *age
. twoway (scatter mgale age) (lowess mgale age)
{res}{txt}
{com}. * Age: the lowess line is close to flat (about -0.07 to +0.06) and rises slowly from about age 40, with the left end based on very few patients; if categorized, age will be split at 45, ignoring the sparse left end
. 
. 
